  "independentScore": {
    "score": 68,
    "scale": "0-100 visual fidelity to the art bible and study-kit language",
    "scorer": "independent reviewer agent (separate from the authoring agent; did not build the asset)",
    "date": "2026-11-16",
    "acceptanceBar": 80,
    "clearsBar": false,
    "rubric": [
      {
        "criterion": "form, layout and proportions",
        "points": 21,
        "max": 30,
        "note": "10x10x4 m box with coffered beam ceiling, walnut wainscot and four offset 1.6 m doors; proportions sit right for a seated 1.6 m probe. It is a plain rectangle with no alcove, niche, arch or hearth recess. The study benchmark is also a box but fills its walls with bookcases, while the hall walls are bare wallpaper above the wainscot."
      },
      {
        "criterion": "signature features: gathering space",
        "points": 15,
        "max": 25,
        "note": "Gear chandelier, brass compass floor inlay, two benches, one stained-glass lancet and two floor candelabra. That is thin for a gathering space. The template has no hearth, table or rug (hearth and rug are runtime dressing), so the floor area reads empty in p5-rooms-hall-hero.jpg."
      },
      {
        "criterion": "surface detail and material read",
        "points": 14,
        "max": 20,
        "note": "Lightmap is clean: 68.6 px/m mean against the study's 66.3, coverage 0.742, no visible seams at the north/west door joins (seam-north, seam-west-turned). Kit-wide deduction: lightmap-only over shared tiling sets, where the study ships baked basecolor/normal/ORM from a 124,581-tri high-poly (hall high is 25,115). Walls are one repeating damask with no breakup."
      },
      {
        "criterion": "colour, value and lighting mood",
        "points": 10,
        "max": 15,
        "note": "Palette is on-bible: warm floor RGB 93,71,56, walnut ceiling 84,38,20, stained-glass patch on the floor. Kit/runtime deduction shared with the study (engine/diffuse frame ratio 1.90 vs study 1.89): in engine the floor shows no pools, foreground L=76 against back-floor L=77. The lightmap itself is also flatter than the study (p90/p10 texel ratio 3.96 vs 7.0)."
      },
      {
        "criterion": "readability and comfort at seated VR distance",
        "points": 8,
        "max": 10,
        "note": "Large clean forms, a clear enemy lane at 2-2.5 m, and a chandelier above head height. The gilt damask is high-contrast near the sconces (L p5 39 to p95 149), which is busy at the periphery."
      }
    ],
    "topFixes": [
      "Add a role anchor to the template: a fireplace recess or long table zone with its own baked warm pool, so the gathering read does not depend on runtime dressing.",
      "Break up the wall plane with bookcase or panelled bays and one niche per wall, so it matches the study's dense walls; the wallpaper should cover far less area.",
      "Restore floor value falloff: the bake p90/p10 is 3.96 against the study's 7.0, so tighten sconce falloff and darken the corners, then fix the kit-wide engine exposure/env flattening."
    ],
    "method": "Looked at (2026-11-16): docs/art-bible.md; PRD.md lightmap contract (lines 87-95); assets-source/concepts/room-sheet-1.png, room-sheet-2.png; study benchmark assets-source/rooms/study/staging/review-sheet.jpg + provenance.json + engine-compare.json; docs/verification/p5-int-study.jpg; assets-source/rooms/hall/provenance.json, staging/review-sheet.jpg, staging/engine-compare.json, staging/hall.lightmap.png (texel stats), docs/verification/p5-rooms-hall-*.jpg and p5-int-hall*.jpg; Pillow crops and region means under /tmp/rxr-score/rooms/."
  }
